@startuml
title Native teammate communication and lifecycle

skinparam shadowing false

actor Operator
participant "Claude lead" as Lead
database "Claude team store" as Store
participant "Claude provider" as Provider
participant "External-team extension" as Extension
participant "Codex thread" as Codex
participant "Codex TUI" as TUI

Lead -> Store : create roster entry and initial assignment
Lead -> Provider : launch via teammate command argv
Provider -> Store : resolve identity, parent, assignment
Provider -> Extension : ExternalMessage(NEW_TASK)
Extension -> Codex : Op::InterAgentCommunication(trigger_turn=true)
Codex -> Codex : queue mailbox and start native turn
Codex -> TUI : stream agent/tool events

Operator -> TUI : optional direct text
TUI -> Codex : TurnInput::UserInput

Lead -> Store : SendMessage(correction)
Store -> Provider : filesystem event/reconciliation
Provider -> Provider : validate and skip journaled ID
Provider -> Extension : ExternalMessage(MESSAGE)
Extension -> Codex : Op::InterAgentCommunication(trigger_turn=true)
Codex --> Extension : submission accepted
Extension -> Provider : journal message ID

alt Codex is working
  Codex -> Codex : deliver at native mailbox boundary
else Codex is idle
  Codex -> Codex : start native turn
end

Codex -> Extension : send_message(target=team-lead)
Extension -> Provider : provider.send_message
Provider -> Store : append native Claude envelope
Store -> Lead : native automatic delivery

Codex -> Extension : final turn item and idle lifecycle
Extension -> Provider : final result + idle notification
Provider -> Store : verified native envelopes
Store -> Lead : result and idle event

Lead -> Store : shutdown request / remove roster entry
Store -> Provider : lifecycle event
Provider -> Provider : validate request + parent authority
Provider -> Store : matching shutdown_response
Provider -> Codex : Op::Shutdown
Codex -> TUI : terminated

note right of Provider
  Claude inbox records remain owned by Claude.
  Codex does not mark or drain them.
end note
@enduml
